Li and $\mathrm{Mg}$ do not form solid bicarbonate, but react with $\mathrm{N}_{2}$ to give nitrides.

$\begin{array}{l}

6 \mathrm{Li}+\mathrm{N}_{2} \stackrel{\Delta}{\rightarrow} 2 \mathrm{Li}_{3} \mathrm{~N} \\

3 \mathrm{Mg}+\mathrm{N}_{2} \stackrel{\Delta}{\rightarrow} \mathrm{Mg}_{3} \mathrm{~N}_{2}

\end{array}$

$\mathrm{CaCl}_{2}$ is produced as a byproduct in solvay ammonia process.



\begin{array}{l}

\text { (i) } \mathrm{NaCl}+\mathrm{CO}_{2}+\mathrm{NH}_{3}+\mathrm{H}_{2} \mathrm{O} \\

\longrightarrow \mathrm{NaHCO}_{3}+\mathrm{NH}_{4} \mathrm{Cl}

\end{array}



(I) $\mathrm{CaCO}_{3} \longrightarrow \mathrm{CO}_{2}+\mathrm{CaO}2 \mathrm{NH}_{2} \mathrm{Cl}+\mathrm{CaO} \longrightarrow 2 \mathrm{NH}_{3}+$

\mathrm{CaCl}_{2}+\mathrm{H}_{2} \mathrm{C}



